\nConclusion: Multiples do NOT independently justify $124; they require margin stability and continuing deleveraging. This is why the scenario probability weights matter.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n\u2022 Competitive response: If TIGO's FMC playbook keeps winning, Claro/Movistar will retaliate with pricing (Chile already proves this template). Impact: \u22122.\n\u2022 Reflexivity: Positive loop already visible \u2014 deleveraging \u2192 lower risk premium \u2192 +142% 12M return [Aggregator] \u2192 cheaper equity for M&A and a stronger eFCF narrative. This cuts both ways: a bad quarter could reverse the rerating.\n\u2022 Customer evolution: Prepaid\u2192postpaid migration (+31% postpaid base [Company]) and FMC 40% penetration raise LTV and lower churn; but FMC's payoff is backloaded and not assured past early adopters.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1/2. Scenario table (probabilities sum to 100%):\n| Scenario | Prob | Key assumptions | Price |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 25% | EBITDA margin fades to 40%, Chile price war spreads, capex 14% of revenue, WACC 11.5%, g 1.5%; leverage >3.0x | $65 |\n| Central | 50% | eFCF guidance met, deleveraging <2.5x, margin ~44%, WACC 10.0%, g 2.25% | $124 |\n| Bull | 25% | Synergies beat, Chile stabilizes, FMC/B2B digital scales, leverage \u21922.0x, WACC 9.0%, margin 46% | $165 |\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update: Prior (base rate for successful large-telco integration) ~55% \u2192 Likelihood (Q2 record eFCF, raised guidance, leverage at 2.73x despite M&A) ~74% \u2192 Posterior \u2248 65% success-weighted; reflected in central 50% + bull 25% (75% non-bear). This is intentionally below 1.5x base rate.\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected price and MoS:\nExpected price = 0.25\u00d765 + 0.50\u00d7124 + 0.25\u00d7165 = $119.50\n50% CI: $92-$140; 80% CI: $65-$165\nMoS vs current $93.68 = (119.50 \u2212 93.68)/119.50 = 21.6% \u2192 ADEQUATE.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nMarket-implied horizon \u2248 2 years (consensus 12-mo target $96.64 \u2248 current price [Aggregator]; price sits at 15.5x FY27E EPS). My horizon is 3-5 years (FY2028-30 eFCF ramp). Spread \u2248 +2-3 years \u2192 moderate arbitrage exists, but only if margin stability holds. Do not extend horizon beyond 2028 without quarterly confirmation.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nConviction Score (15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 (wide moat, 46.3% EBITDA margin)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 2/3 (21.6% MoS on expected value, but WACC-sensitive)\n3. Macro alignment: 1.5/3 (headwind \u22120.5)\n4. Thesis clarity / KPIs: 2.5/3 (eFCF, leverage, organic revenue are all measurable)\n5. Execution traceability: 2.5/3 (record Q2, raised guide; but Q1 EPS miss)\nTotal: 11.5/15 \u2192 HIGH conviction. Conviction decay: \u22121 point per 6 months absent confirmation.\nSizing guideline: High conviction \u2192 8-12% max, but apply caps: Engine 1 leveraged incumbent (\u22122p), macro headwind (\u22121p), crowding (\u22121p) \u2192 Final max weight \u2248 8%.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n\u2022 Short interest 4.19% of float, down 12.4% MoM [Aggregator] \u2014 no squeeze fuel; shorts are covering.\n\u2022 Institutional ownership 49.7%; insider 46.1% [Aggregator] \u2014 small float; price moves amplified; potential PE overhang on any unwind.\n\u2022 12M return +142% [Aggregator]; price near 52-wk high $107.13 [Aggregator] \u2014 momentum positive but sentiment elevated.\n\u2022 Crowding risk score: 8/15 \u2014 moderate; reduce position size by 1p.\n\u2022 Options positioning: no data [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nTIGO is an EM-telecom/defensive-growth hybrid: low correlation to US large-cap (beta 0.904), high correlation to EM currencies and USD rates. It fits a portfolio under-allocated to LatAm or EM cash-generative assets. If the book is already EM-heavy, add no more than 4% and hedge COP/GTQ/PYG exposure partially. Avoid pairing with other USD-debt EM names (see 7.5).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\nFull-Kelly (continuous approximation): \u03bc = +27.6% expected return (to $119.50); \u03c3\u00b2 from scenario distribution \u2248 0.117 \u2192 f* \u2248 \u03bc/\u03c3\u00b2 \u2248 2.36 \u2014 far too large; apply fractional Kelly 1/8 \u2192 29%. After model-risk haircuts (LatAm FX, leverage, data unreliability, macro headwind) \u2192 6%. Gap vs Layer 5 cap (8%) is 2p \u2014 within the 20p limit. Final initial size: 5%; scale to 6-8% only on confirmation of FY26 eFCF \u2265 $1.1B.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nCatalysts (0-6 months): Q3'26 results (Nov 2026) post-print; FY2026 eFCF \u2265$1.1B confirmation; year-end leverage <2.5x; preliminary FY2027 guidance (Q4 call); Chile/Ecuador margin commentary; January/April 2027 dividend payment.\nCatalysts (6-18 months): final Colombia integration benefits; B2B digital (cloud/cybersecurity) scale; potential further deleveraging-driven multiple expansion.\n\nRisks: (1) Chile price war; (2) Colombia competitive response (Claro/Movistar); (3) FX devaluation (COP, GTQ, PYG, BOB) vs USD debt; (4) regulatory/legal (Guatemala DPA precedent \u2014 $118M paid [Actual/DOJ]); (5) integration execution; (6) interest-rate resurgence; (7) rising D&A burden if capex is misallocated; (8) insider/PE overhang.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\nTIGO's bear triggers (USD strength, EM risk-off, LatAm FX) correlate with other EM positions in a stress episode. Historical tail correlation to EM equities \u2248 0.7 [Assumption]. Conditional VaR (5%, 1-year): a 2008/2020-style EM freeze would drop TIGO roughly 40-50% (to $47-56) regardless of fundamentals. Reduce gross exposure by the crowding haircut already applied; consider offsetting with a long-USD/short-COP hedge if unhedged EM exposure is already high.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\nThesis KPIs (Quarterly):\n1. FY2026 eFCF \u2265 $1.1B [Company guidance] \u2014 integrity fail if < $800M.\n2.