IGO is a leveraged short-USD trade.\n5. The Guatemala DPA ($118M) demonstrates a governance discount that deserves a permanent lower multiple.\n6. The 3-yr share issuance CAGR of +5.9% means equity holders have been diluted to fund the strategy.\n7. Net profit attributable to owners fell 83.9% YoY in Q2'26 to $109M [Research brief] \u2014 the \"record cash flow\" narrative masks a bottom-line that is still weak.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic combat: Long strength 7/10; Short strength 6.5/10. Gap = 0.5 < 2 \u2192 conviction capped at HIGH, not VERY HIGH. Position size and scale-in rules reflect this.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: DOJ/Guatemala settlement is [Actual] (justice.gov). No active Hindenburg-type report on TIGO [Unconfirmed]. The pack itself warns that fiscal-year trending is unreliable (basis-change risk) \u2014 the FY2022 revenue step (+32%) is unverified and may be a tag change, not an event.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments:\n\u2022 \"FCF growth makes it cheap\" \u2014 KILLED at WACC >11.5% ($98) or terminal margin <38% ($95). Re-visit if FY26 eFCF \u2265 $1.1B confirmed AND leverage <2.5x.\n\u2022 \"FMC is a platform moat\" \u2014 KILLED if penetration stalls at 40%; currently only a churn/lifetime-value support.\n\u2022 \"Deleveraging is guaranteed\" \u2014 KILLED by a single major FX shock; re-validate quarterly (net debt and FX).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\nSelected mandatory checks (full 37-point framework applied):\nA. Methodology: \u2713 Engine 1 chosen for archetype A; no DCF-only conclusion \u2014 cross-checked with multiples and eFCF.\nB. Valuation: \u2713 Forecast years beyond FY2027 flagged as [Assumption]; sensitivity shown; WACC, terminal g, and margins all disclosed with ranges.\nC. Bias: \u2713 Anchoring to the +142% momentum was tested by the WACC 11.5% / low-margin scenario ($95 \u2248 market). Overconfidence check: scenario weights deliberately not tilted.\nD. Consistency: \u2713 Time points respected; FY2025 GAAP net income not used as