2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nR&D capitalisation: N/A (telecom; minimal R&D).\nSBC treatment: FY25 SBC $14M [Actual] \u2014 de minimis (0.2% of revenue). No material adjustment.\nLease capitalisation: FY25 operating leases $2.587B [Actual] \u2014 already inside company\n  net-debt figure ($8.075B H1-26 [Actual]). No further adjustment.\nBrand/data asset estimate: Tigo brand in LatAm, but not recurring-saleable; no reliable\n  value add. NOT capitalised \u2014 conservatism. [Assumption]\nOwner Earnings (FY25, Buffett style): NI $1.362B + D&A 1.280 \u2212 maintenance capex 0.650\n  \u2212 \u0394WC (not derivable) = ~$1.99B; but NI includes $604M one-off Lati gain (pre-tax)\n  [Actual] \u2192 normalised owner earnings ~$1.5B [Estimate].\nConclusion: GAAP vs adjusted ROIC gap not material for a capital-intensive regulated\n  business; no >5%p divergence. [Assumption]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 1 \u2014 TRADITIONAL DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nENTERPRISE CLASSIFICATION (Layer 0): Archetype A (Stable Incumbent) with transition\n  triggers toward B (Quality Compounder). Rationale: (1) recurring subscription revenue,\n  (2) high OCF stability ($1.2\u20131.7B over 10 yrs [Actual]), (3) government-regulated\n  essential service, (4) improving margins/FCF conversion. Transition criteria: FCF+\n  for 2 consecutive quarters achieved; ROIC > WACC for 3 years NOT yet demonstrated\n  \u2192 50\u201380% of criteria met \u2192 BLENDED ENGINE: Engine 1 (DCF+Multiples) \u00d7 75% +\n  Engine 4 (Expectation/Valuation-Bridge) \u00d7 25% to value the integration optionality.\n  Errors avoided vs alternatives: Engine 2 (Cyclical) inappropriate because demand is\n  non-cyclical; Engine 4 alone would over-weight the integration option; Engine 3\n  (Product-Platform) does not apply (no hardware installed base).\n\nDiscount-rate derivation (WACC):\n  - Risk-free: 4.71% (10Y UST, 21-Aug-26) [Actual \u2014 market]\n  - Equity risk premium: 5.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run DM ERP + EM lift]\n  - Beta: 1.05 [Assumption \u2014 vendor says 0.904 with unstated window; leverage 2.7x\n    and LatAm FX justify \u22651.0]\n  - Cost of equity = 4.71 + 1.05 \u00d7 5.5 = 10.49% [Arithmetic]\n  - Pre-tax cost of debt: 6.5% [Estimate \u2014 H1-26 interest expense $516M / avg net debt\n    ~$8.2B \u2248 6.3\u20136.6%; vendor total debt supports same ballpark]\n  - After-tax cost of debt: 6.5 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.25) = 4.87% [Assumption \u2014 25% tax rate,\n    because pack's tax inputs are PROVABLY BROKEN (Layer 8)]\n  - Debt weight: 34% (8.08 / (15.71 + 8.08)); equity weight: 66% [Arithmetic]\n  - WACC = 0.66 \u00d7 10.49 + 0.34 \u00d7 4.87 = 8.58% \u2192 ROUND 8.6%\n\nForecast \u2014 BASE CASE (explicit years FY2026\u20132030):\n| ($B)          | 2026E | 2027E | 2028E | 2029E | 2030E |\n| Revenue       | 8.35  | 8.68  | 9.03  | 9.34  | 9.62  |\n| EBITDA mgn    | 45.0% | 46.0% | 47.0% | 47.5% | 48.0% |\n| EBITDA        | 3.76  | 3.99  | 4.24  | 4.44  | 4.62  |\n| D&A           | 1.95  | 1.90  | 1.85  | 1.80  | 1.75  |\n| EBIT          | 1.81  | 2.09  | 2.39  | 2.64  | 2.87  |\n| NOPAT (25%)   | 1.36  | 1.57  | 1.79  | 1.98  | 2.15  |\n| Capex         | 1.00  | 0.95  | 0.95  | 0.93  | 0.91  |\n| \u0394WC           | (0.05)| (0.05)| (0.05)| (0.05)| (0.05)|\n| UFCF          | 2.26  | 2.47  | 2.64  | 2.80  | 2.94  |\n\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE on forecast drivers:\n- FY2026 revenue: H1-26 actual $4.164B [Actual] + H2E \u2248 $4.19B [Assumption \u2014 Q2 $2.18B\n  [Actual], flat H2; World Cup H1 boost fades, Ecuador brand-launch drags H2 [Actual call]])\n- FY2027\u201330 revenue growth 4%\u21923%: organic service revenue +5.4% YTD [Actual]; consensus\n  revenue growth +2.96% [Estimate]; my path is ABOVE consensus \u2192 deliberately stress-tested\n  in Layer 4 (base 4%, not 5%). No management FY27 guidance exists [Unconfirmed].\n- EBITDA margin 45%\u219248%: Q2-26 adj. EBITDA margin 46.3% [Actual]; restructuring $160\u2013170M\n  in 2026 fades [Actual]; Coltel synergies [Actual \u2014 management asserts, quantification [Unconfirmed]].\n  Uruguay/FMC scale-up supports. Margin path is MY ASSUMPTION, not guided.\n- D&A: FY25 1.28 [Actual] + PPA amortization from Colombia/Ecuador/Uruguay/Chile adds\n  ~$0.6B in 2026 [Estimate \u2014 H1 OI implies EBIT 1.81 vs EBITDA 3.76]; decays as intangibles\n  amortise. [Assumption]\n- Capex: FY26 = 12% of revenue (management guidance [Actual \u2014 call: \"full-year capex expected\n  ~12% of revenue\"]); 2027\u21929.5%: MY ASSUMPTION, NOT GUIDED. Range tested: 9\u201313%.\n  NOTE: pack capex $650M FY25 [Actual] excludes capitalised software; the vendor's $814M\n  is broader. 12% of $8.35B = $1.00B sits ABOVE both \u2014 conservative and consistent with\n  company guidance.\n- Tax 25%: [Assumption \u2014 pack's tax field is provably broken; LatAm statutory ~25\u201335%;\n  25% is the middle of the plausible range and is a deliberate uncertainty carried in scenarios.\n- Terminal growth 2.5%: [Assumption] \u2264 long-run LatAm nominal GDP (~4\u20135%) discounted for\n  telecom maturity; conservative.\n- Terminal multiple 6.0x EV/EBITDA: [Assumption] = LatAm telecom comps (Am\u00e9rica M\u00f3vil ~5.5,\n  Telef\u00f3nica ~5, Liberty LatAm ~5 [Tier 3 \u2014 Estimate]). Also stress at 5.5x and 7x.\n\nDiscounting at 8.6%:\n  PV UFCF 2026\u201330: 2.08 + 2.10 + 2.06 + 2.01 + 1.95 = 10.20 [Arithmetic]\n  Terminal value: 6.0 \u00d7 4.62 = 27.72; PV = 27.72 / 1.510 = 18.36 [Arithmetic]\n  EV = 28.56 | Less net debt 8.08 [Actual] | Equity = 20.48 | Per share = $122.1\n  \u2192 BASE IV = $122 (rounded)\n\nMultiples cross-check (Engine 1 discipline \u2014 no DCF-only conclusion):\n  - Forward EV/EBITDA 6.3x (EV 23.8 / EBITDA 3.76) vs comps 5\u20137.5x \u2192 middle-to-cheap [Arithmetic]\n  - Dividend yield 4.8% (4.50/93.68) [Actual]; eFCF yield 7.0% (1.1/15.7) [Arithmetic]\n  - P/E distorted by one-offs; not used. [Actual \u2014 FY25 included $604M Lati gain]\n  - EV/Revenue ~2.85x [Arithmetic]\n\nTornado \u2014 top 3 value drivers:\n  1. FY2030 EBITDA margin (range 44%\u219248%): IV moves approx $95 \u2192 $145\n  2. Terminal EV/EBITDA multiple (5x\u21927x): IV moves approx $95 \u2192 $145\n  3. Capex intensity post-2027 (13%\u21929%): IV moves approx $105 \u2192 $135\n  These three become Thesis KPIs (Layer 7).\n\nReverse DCF check: current price $93.68 implies exiting 6.2x EV/EBITDA on 2030 EBITDA of\n  ~$4.1B with WACC 8.6% \u2014 i.e., the market already prices only modest margin expansion to\n  ~46.5% and capex staying ~11%. Market is NOT pricing the full integration success case;\n  it is pricing \"solid execution, no blow-up\". [Arithmetic]\n\nENGINE 4 25% blend (integration optionality): Coltel/Ecuador/Uruguay synergies at 40%\n  probability of full delivery [+$0.4B EBITDA by 2028], 40% partial, 20% failure \u2192 option\n  value \u2248 $3.5B \u2192 +$1.5B equity after discounting \u2248 +$9/share [Assumption].\n  BLENDED IV = 0.75 \u00d7 122 + 0.25 \u00d7 (122 + 9) = 91.5 + 32.75 = $124.3 \u2248 $124.\n  (Blend raises IV modestly; use $124 as the technical base before Layer-4 scenario weights.)\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1. Competitive response: Claro, Movistar aggressive in Colombia \u2014 already visible\n  (churn, promo). If TIGO's postpaid migration succeeds, expects counter-moves:\n  \u22121 (mildly negative) in FY27 margins. [Estimate]\n3.5-2. Reflexivity (positive): higher stock price \u2192 SBC attraction (small), cheaper\n  M&A currency, improved supplier terms. Also reduced refinancing risk perception.\n  [Estimate]\n3.5-3. Customer evolution: FMC penetration 40% [Actual] rising toward 60% [Assumption];\n  home services + World Cup packages pushed ARPU; B2B digital +14% [Actual] \u2014 each\n  extends customer lifetime value. LTV/CAC trends [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (base rate): post-M&A value creation success ~50% [Layer 1.5]\nPosterior update: earnings evidence (H1 OCF $1.30B, eFCF +56%, raised guidance [Actual])\n  raises success likelihood. Posterior P(success) \u2248 55\u201360% [Estimate].\n\nScenarios (must sum 100%; high > base? NO \u2014 single highest is BASE):\n  BEAR (25%): Integration stumbles; Chile price war; Bolivia FX crisis pushes USD-debt\n              burden up; EBITDA margin fades to 44%; capex stays 12%+; terminal 5.0x.\n              \u2192 IV \u2248 $74 (per detailed bear DCF: 8.37 + 12.1 \u2212 8.08 = 12.4B equity) [Arithmetic]\n  BASE (50%): Organic growth +4\u21923%, margin 45\u219247%, capex 12\u219210%, exit 6.0x \u2192 IV \u2248 $122 [Arithmetic]\n  BULL (25%): Synergies deliver early; margin 48% by 2029; capex 9.5%; exit 7.0x; FX stable\n              \u2192 IV \u2248 $150 (explicit PV 10.2 + TV 21.4 \u2212 8.1 + engine-4 upside) [Arithmetic]\n\nProbability-weighted = 0.25\u00d774 + 0.50\u00d7122 + 0.25\u00d7150 = 18.5 + 61.0 + 37.5 = $117 [Arithmetic]\n\u2192 FAIR VALUE \u2248 $115\u2013117. Use $115 as conservative central point.\n50% CI: $98\u2013$135 [Estimate \u2014 based on scenario distribution and model errors]\n80% CI: $75\u2013$155 [Estimate]\n\nMargin of Safety: (115 \u2212 93.68) / 115 = 18.5% \u2192 ADEQUATE band (15\u201330%).\nExpected price: $115; but scenarios are not symmetric \u2014 skew is to the UPSIDE ($150 vs $74).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: reverse-DCF at $93.68 implies the market capitalises only\n  ~3 years of the normalised FCF path and applies a 6.2x exit \u2014 effectively horizon\n  \u2248 2028E, with no credit for post-2028 FCF growth beyond 2.5%. [Arithmetic]\nMy horizon: 3\u20135 years (default).\nSpread: ~1\u20132 years. Arbitrage exists, but is moderate, not extreme (max 2-yr spread);\n  position sizing reflects this (4.5%, not 8%).\n\n\u2500\u