rate\n     environment; eFCF $1.1B covers the dividend $0.75B but leaves only $0.35B for\n     deleveraging \u2014 \"guided deleveraging\" is largely dividend-financed optimism.\n  4. Bolivia new FX regime is an uncontrolled variable; Guatemala has $296M legal\n     claims with only $47M provisioned after a $118M bribery DPA.\n  5. Record margins (Paraguay 56.9%) are mean-reverting; Colombia/Chile competition\n     is intensifying; Ecuador brand-launch costs hit H2.\n  6. The turnaround story has been \"one quarter away\" before: Q1-26 EPS $0.65 vs\n     expected $0.85 (miss [Actual \u2014 web brief]).\n  7. 6.3x EV/EBITDA is not cheap for LatAm telecoms \u2014 Am\u00e9rica M\u00f3vil trades at ~5.5x\n     with a stronger balance sheet.\n\nLogic combat (Long vs Short):\n  Long logic strength: 13/20 \u2014 grounded in actual eFCF, guided FCF step-up, real MoS.\n  Short logic strength: 11/20 \u2014 valid on leverage/FX, but misses that the market has\n  ALREADY discounted much of it (6.3x multiple, analyst target only +3%).\n  Gap = 2 \u2192 conviction \u22120.5 step (already applied).\n\nAdversarial data: Hindenburg/activist reports: NONE found [Unconfirmed \u2014 no campaign].\n  DPA history is the effective adversarial evidence [Actual \u2014 DOJ 2024].\nKilled arguments (with resurrection conditions):\n  - \"eFCF guidance is just timing (H1 +56% partly due to expense timing [call])\" \u2014\n    KILLED for 2026 because guidance was RAISED from \u2265$900M to ~$1.1B. RESURRECT if\n    Q3-26 eFCF < $250M.\n  - \"Insider 46% = confident\" \u2014 KILLED as a positive because it is structure (Millicom\n    controlling family), not fresh buying. RESURRECT only on actual Form-4 cluster buying.\n  - \"Dividend 4.8% is safe\" \u2014 CHALLENGED: payout 68% of eFCF with deleveraging target.\n    Acceptable but high. RESURRECT as a RED FLAG if leverage >3x at YE26.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\