HECKLIST:\n  Q1 2026 (already reported): Missed EPS $0.65 vs $0.85 \u2014 explainable\n  (restructuring); eFCF trajectory intact.\n  Q3/Q4 2026: eFCF pacing, World Cup fade impact, leverage exit rate.\n\n  PRE-MORTEM (Step 7-4) \u2014 \"If TIGO fails in 5 years, why?\"\n  1. FAILURE-MODE A: Colombia price war \u2192 EBITDA $3.0B, leverage 3.5x,\n     dividend cut. Early-warning: Claro aggressive prepaid pricing,\n     Tigo prepaid net-adds negative for 3+ quarters.\n  2. FAILURE-MODE B: capex trap \u2192 5G/fiber capacity requires 16% capex\n     intensity; eFCF drops to $400-500M. Early-warning: capex guidance\n     >$1.3B with no commensurate ARPU.\n  3. FAILURE-MODE C: FX cascade (COP/GTQ -20%) \u2192 USD revenue flat,\n     dollar-debt burden rises, leverage 3.2x. Early-warning: DXY rally,\n     LatAm populist fiscal stress.\n\n  DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY (Step 7-5):\n  T0 $93.68; IV $154 (prob-weighted); Base IV $160; key assumptions:\n  capex 13%, tax 22%, WACC 9.5%; red-team gap 0.4 \u2192 conviction 11.5/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM \u2014 ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n  SHORT THESIS (using the same data):\n  1. The $1.1B eFCF guidance is a peak: 2026 benefits from World Cup\n     top-ups/advertising, favorable expense timing, and working-capital\n     timing. Normalized eFCF is ~$800M.\n  2. 45-46% EBITDA margins are not sustainable \u2014 Chile is a price war,\n     Colombia's post-Coltel churn is masked by a reporting harmonization;\n     Ecuador margins contract in H2-26 per CFO.\n  3. The FY25 net income of $1.362B contains one-off gains (tower sales,\n     FX) \u2014 not a $8+ EPS run-rate; normalized EPS is ~$4-5.\n  4. LatAm FX will revert to the 2016-2021 pattern \u2014 USD revenue was FLAT\n     for six years. A 10-15% COP/GTQ decline cuts USD EBITDA 10-15%.\n  5. Multiple is already at the top of LatAm peers (6.1x vs 4.5-5.5x).\n     The market is paying for a rerating BEFORE it has been earned.\n  6. M&A base rate is against them: 70% of large EM telecom M&A fails to\n     create value; Millicom's own history (2023 goodwill impairment, $245M\n     loss) is the evidence.\n  7. Governance: a $118M DPA in Guatemala is a warning, not a one-off;\n     other LatAm jurisdictions may have exposures.\n\n  LOGIC COMBAT:\n  Long: 4.2/5   Short: 3.8/5   GAP: 0.4 \u2192 Conviction -0.5 steps\n  (incorporated in Section 5).\n\n  ADVERSARIAL DATA: DOJ Guatemala resolution [Actual \u2014 Justice.gov] is the\n  only named adversarial data point; Hindenburg-style reports: none\n  identified in research window [Unconfirmed].\n\n  KILLED ARGUMENTS (when they could come back):\n  \u2022 \"Colombia integration is clean\" \u2014 REVIVES if Claro launches a price war\n    (watch Colombia ARPU).\n  \u2022 \"Capex 13% is the new normal\" \u2014 REVIVES if a 2027-28 5G/fiber cycle is\n    announced with >$1.4B guidance.\n  \u2022 \"Tax rate ~20%\" \u2014 REVIVES if LatAm governments widen tax bases; the\n    pack's tax inputs are broken, so this estimate carries more weight than\n    I would like.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  A. Methodology: PASS \u2014 no DCF-only, no multiple-only, no narrative-only\n     conclusion; macro, base rates, positioning, and red team all included.\n  B. Valuation audit: PASS \u2014 DCF cross-checked with EV/EBITDA, P/E, eFCF\n     yield, and the analyst-target range; IV deltas explained.\n  C. Bias audit: PASS with note \u2014 the analyst started with a positive view;\n     the base-rate check (Layer 1.5) and the 30% Bear weight are the\n     explicit counterweights.\n  D. Consistency audit: PASS \u2014 no T0/T-1/Tpf mixing; no GAAP/IFRS mixing\n     (data-packs flags respected); FY26 revenue basis change flagged and\n     handled as a scale reset.\n  E. Narrative audit: PASS \u2014 no \"large long-term potential\" language;\n     every driver traced to a data-pack line or a cited external source.\n  F. Red-team audit: PASS \u2014 Section 9 completed; the gap is disclosed.\n  G. Data-integrity audit: CONDITIONAL PASS \u2014\n     FAILED ITEMS: (1) tax inputs provably broken for 6/10 years \u2014\n     tax rate is [Assumption]; (2) working capital data absent \u2014 \u0394WC is\n     [Assumption]; (3) no TTM / no segment detail \u2014 FY26E revenue and\n     EBITDA are [Estimate]; (4) operating-lease/overlap ambiguity \u2014 the\n     vendor debt figure is used as the authoritative cross-check.\n     These failed items do not invalidate the conclusion; they are already\n     embedded in the wide 80% CI ($60-$235).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  DATE: 2026-08-24\n  PRICE: $93.68 | IV: $154 (prob-weighted) | MoS: 39%\n  SCENARIOS: Bear 30% / Base 45% / Bull 25% \u2192 $99 / $160 / $210\n  KEY ASSUMPTIONS: WACC 9.5%; FY26E EBITDA $3.87B; capex 13% of revenue;\n  cash tax 22%; terminal g 2.5%; Coltel/Ecuador synergies landing per Q2-26\n  evidence.\n  RED-TEAM CONCERN: Market already pays a premium multiple; earnings quality\n  (World Cup, timing, one-offs) is the main risk; capex reversion would\n  break the thesis. FX is the uncontrolled variable.\n  CONVICTION: 11.5/15 (High). POSITION: 6% target, 3 tranches.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nACTION     : BUY / ACCUMULATE (not a full-position, not a leveraged bet).\nCONVICTION : HIGH (11.5/15)\nTARGET POSITION: 6.0% of portfolio (max 7%);\n                 if the book already carries EM/FX risk, use 5.0%.\nENTRY STRATEGY (split entry \u2014 mandatory given macro headwind):\n  Tranche 1: 50% of intended position at market ($93.68).\n  Tranche 2: 30% on a pullback to $85 (-9%, near analyst-min cluster).\n  Tranche 3: 20% at $72-75 (-22%) (the 80%-CI lower-ish zone).\n  If Q4-26 or Q1-27 confirms eFCF at/above $1.1B and leverage <2.5x,\n   the tranche-2 limit can be lifted to $90.\nEXIT / RE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS:\n  Breach of TWO monitoring criteria (Section 8) \u2192 full re-analysis.\n  Hard fundamental stop: FY26 eFCF < $900M OR capex/revenue > 15% in FY27\n   guidance \u2192 exit or cut to 2%.\nTIME HORIZON: 3-5 years. EXPECTED RETURN: ~+20-30% IRR at entry, excluding\n  the 3.2% dividend.\nTARGET PRICE (12-24 month): $120-150 (Base-to-expected), a +28% to +60%\n  move from T0.\n\nFINAL WORD: TIGO offers a genuine asymmetry \u2014 the market is pricing the\nstagnant outcome while the Q2-2026 evidence points to a cash-flow\ninflection. T